From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:17:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: wait for the ledger before a scanless join's
 commands

The first roams failed: the re-arm finished, the scanless join sent its
first command under a millisecond later, and that command returned -EBUSY
(mask-control status=-16). The error ended the lifetime and restarted the
firmware. A scan never met this, since it comes well after the re-arm.

Wait for the ledger to go idle first, within the existing bound.

Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 4.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c | 30 +++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
index ebdf99563..520d08e90 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
@@ -921,6 +921,19 @@ static int mt6797_mac_lifetime_begin(struct mt6797_mac *mac)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int mt6797_mac_await_idle(struct mt6797_mac *mac, u64 end)
+{
+	int ret = 0;
+
+	while (!ret && !mt6797_hif_normal_idle(mac->hif)) {
+		if (ktime_get_ns() >= end)
+			return -ETIMEDOUT;
+		usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+		ret = mt6797_mac_scan_guard(mac, end);
+	}
+	return ret;
+}
+
 /* A join from an earlier scan's results, as in a roam: open the lifetime a scan
  * would have left. Called with the mutex held, on a re-armed idle driver.
  */
@@ -936,15 +949,16 @@ int mt6797_mac_join_open_lifetime(struct mt6797_mac *mac)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	if (!mac->sequence_base)
 		mac->sequence_base = mac->sequence;
-	ret = mt6797_mac_lifetime_begin(mac);
-	/* The peer commands start from an idle ledger, as after a scan. */
+	/* The re-arm can leave the cleanup's last pages unreconciled, and a
+	 * command then returns -EBUSY, which would end this lifetime.
+	 */
 	end = ktime_get_ns() + 500 * NSEC_PER_MSEC;
-	while (!ret && !mt6797_hif_normal_idle(mac->hif)) {
-		if (ktime_get_ns() >= end)
-			ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
-		else
-			ret = mt6797_mac_scan_guard(mac, end);
-	}
+	ret = mt6797_mac_await_idle(mac, end);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = mt6797_mac_lifetime_begin(mac);
+	/* The peer commands start from an idle ledger, as after a scan. */
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = mt6797_mac_await_idle(mac, ktime_get_ns() + 500 * NSEC_PER_MSEC);
 	if (ret) {
 		if (!mac->first_error)
 			mac->first_error = ret;
-- 
2.43.0

